WEBVTT

00:00:01.880 --> 00:00:05.710
This is the Singularity Daily, for Wednesday, November 4.

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:10.010
Here's your day in superintelligence, in 3 minutes flat.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:16.420
It's building itself.

00:00:16.420 --> 00:00:21.000
Anthropic told investors its AI may soon speed up its own progress.

00:00:22.030 --> 00:00:25.610
And it's reportedly using Claude to help design its own chips.

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:38.370
At MIT, GPT-6 Astra rewrote the numbers inside another AI. No retraining.

00:00:39.380 --> 00:00:43.550
It changed a tiny sliver of them, and the maths score jumped sixfold.

00:00:45.940 --> 00:00:51.430
Baidu's new simulator gives robotaxis up to 100,000 km of practice a day.

00:00:52.970 --> 00:00:56.400
CrowdStrike launched a kill switch for AI agents.

00:00:56.400 --> 00:00:59.350
If one goes rogue, it's stopped anywhere.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:04.530
Now, the money. CrowdStrike is also buying two AI security startups,

00:01:04.530 --> 00:01:06.800
for about half a billion dollars.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:08.360
In England,

00:01:08.360 --> 00:01:14.170
Drax and Brookfield plan a $27 billion AI data centre at a power station.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:17.890
And Anthropic's listing, due this month,

00:01:17.890 --> 00:01:21.290
could value it near $1.5 trillion, reportedly.

00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:25.380
Samsung will reportedly make memory chip part

00:01:25.380 --> 00:01:28.260
s for AMD and Nvidia at a second Texas plant.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:32.800
Meanwhile, Apple Watch is testing Siri Recap.

00:01:32.800 --> 00:01:36.210
It turns your conversations into notes, if you opt in.

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:40.580
Missed what someone just said? Double-press the crown,

00:01:40.580 --> 00:01:42.740
and it shows you the last 15 seconds.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:49.500
The catch? Schools that block Google's AI lose Search for students too.

00:01:49.690 --> 00:01:55.580
And Britain's cyber agency expects AI-powered attacks on vital services by 2028.

00:01:56.720 --> 00:01:58.370
So... is it so over?

00:01:59.060 --> 00:02:00.450
We're so back!

00:02:01.880 --> 00:02:02.760
Now, machines.

00:02:02.760 --> 00:02:08.460
China's BrainCo is building a wearable that could curb appetite by stimulating the brain.

00:02:09.380 --> 00:02:11.940
They call it an electronic weight-loss drug,

00:02:11.940 --> 00:02:14.150
aiming to sell it within three years.

00:02:15.940 --> 00:02:21.140
And Tesla's Cybercabs have joined Waymo, testing robotaxis on Detroit's streets.

00:02:22.500 --> 00:02:24.790
So, it's starting to build itself.

00:02:24.790 --> 00:02:28.230
Even its makers say humans need to stay in charge.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:33.030
Day after day, the curve keeps bending upward.

00:02:33.750 --> 00:02:36.540
And the future keeps arriving ahead of schedule.

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:40.880
One day, all of this. Tomorrow, probably more.

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:47.100
This has been the Singularity Daily.

00:02:48.750 --> 00:02:49.940
See you tomorrow.

00:02:52.500 --> 00:02:56.010
Want the whole month? Hear more on November 27.
